Skia: "[Graphite] Only allow clip path key bounds within int16_t" (crbugs
581669556 and 578656869, not public; no CVE listed yet): Graphite packed a
clip path's unclipped bounds into its cache key as int16_t values without
checking that they fit, and OR'ed in their sign extension, so different
clips could share a key; bounds that don't fit are now keyed by the save
record ID. Skia main commit e6fe4f71440d7f5341acffedb8a8b03b514ef4c9,
merged on 2026-11-04 to Skia's chrome/m157 branch
(c2609d43d1efb837b13fe5e9f355083104e637ce; not yet rolled into the 157
branch) and proposed for chrome/m156. This is that merge, at
third_party/skia/, without its tests. Drop it once a 157 tag's Skia has it.

